  <article class="policy">
  <h1>Tiny Treats Café – Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: 11 November 2026</p>

<p>Tiny Treats Café is a casual cooking game made by an independent developer ("we"). This policy explains what information the game uses on Android (Google Play), on iPhone and iPad (the App Store), and in web browsers (the free demo on itch.io).</p>

<h2>The short version</h2>
<ul>
  <li>We don't ask for your name, email or any account, and we don't run any servers that collect information about you.</li>
  <li>Your game progress is saved only on your own device.</li>
  <li>Purchases are handled by Google Play or Apple's App Store, and optional ads are provided by Google AdMob. Google and Apple collect some information to do this, as described below.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Game progress</h2>
<p>Your progress (day, coins, stars, upgrades and settings) and whether you bought the full game are saved in files on your device, or in your browser's storage when you play on the web. They are never sent to us. Uninstalling the game or clearing your browser's data deletes them. Your device's own backup (if you have it turned on) may include them.</p>

<h2>Purchases (Android, iPhone and iPad)</h2>
<p>The first two bakeries are free; the rest can be unlocked with a one-time purchase through Google Play or the App Store. Payment is handled entirely by Google or Apple: we never see your card or payment details. The game only receives a confirmation that the purchase was made, so it can unlock the bakeries and restore them on a new device. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

<h2>Ads (Android, iPhone and iPad)</h2>
<p>You can choose to watch short video ads to double a day's coins, or to open the next bakery without buying the full game. Ads are only shown when you tap a button to watch one. They are provided by Google AdMob, which may collect and use:</p>
<ul>
  <li>your device's advertising ID and other device identifiers,</li>
  <li>your IP address and approximate location (country or region),</li>
  <li>information about the ads you see and interact with, and about the app,</li>
</ul>
<p>to show ads, measure them and prevent fraud. If you are in a region where the law requires it (such as the European Economic Area, the UK or Switzerland), the game asks for your consent with Google's consent form before any ads are loaded, and you can change your choice at any time with the "Ad privacy choices" button in the game's Settings. On iPhone and iPad, the game also asks Apple's "Allow tracking?" question; if you choose "Ask App Not to Track", the game does not share your device's advertising identifier with AdMob. You can also reset or delete your advertising ID, or change tracking permission, in your device's settings.</p>
<p>Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>.</p>

<h2>The web version</h2>
<p>The free web demo is hosted on itch.io, which has its own <a href="https://itch.io/docs/legal/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>. The web demo has no ads and no purchases.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>The game is suitable for everyone but is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. The ads shown are limited to content suitable for general audiences.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page with a new date.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about privacy in Tiny Treats Café: <a href="mailto:vijaya2798@gmail.com">vijaya2798@gmail.com</a></p>
